/.devcontainer/
/.git/
/dist/

/.dockerignore
/.gitignore
/docker-bake.hcl
/docker-compose.yaml

# wick.yaml is not excluded, though it is mounted at runtime rather than baked
# into the image. It is the documentation, and the tests read it: a file that
# says what may be written and does not itself load is worse than none, and it
# has caught itself out once already.
#
# Nor is .github/ or docs/, for the same reason and a sharper one. modules_test.go
# reads both -- go.work is the list of modules and everything else is checked
# against it, including the two CI loops, the two cache blocks and the release
# tag recipe. CI's only run of the gate is this image, so a check that cannot
# see those files is a check that does not run where it matters.
